{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5","id":1512700,"title":"Core Themes of the Tribes for a better W5","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-25T02:23:31-07:00","id":1512700,"title":"Core Themes of the Tribes for a better W5","content":"So this is just a self-indulgent thought process of HOW to potentially handle the tribes of the Nation better as a reboot without making them overlap with each other.<br /> <br /> This thread is NOT about how bad W5 is, this is about trying to squeeze the tribes into a generalist concept that stands out.<br /> <br /> <br /> Black Furies: The sacred feminity without shackles of progress.<br /> Bone Gnawers: Survival in what others ignore.<br /> Children of Gaia: Healing and Diplomacy.<br /> Fianna: Family in its worst and best aspects.<br /> Fenrir: War and the strength of will.<br /> Glass Walkers: Utopian dreams and mimicry of humanity.<br /> Red Talons: Self-denial and call to ignorance.<br /> Shadow Lords: Staining your hands so others do not have to.<br /> Silent Striders: Haunted and seeking redemption.<br /> Silver Fangs: Entitlement from bloodlines and birth status<br /> Stargazers: Asceticism and contemplation of meaning.<br /> Older Brother: Curiosity killed the cat and satisfaction brought it back.<br /> Younger Brother: Defiance in the face of erasure.<br /> <br /> Black Spiral Dancers: Freedom in being a monster.<br /> Ronin: Refusal of tradition and 'how it has always been done.'<br /> <br /> Note, these are how -I- see the tribes at their core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T02:49:48-07:00","id":1512703,"title":"","content":"Very good concepts. It's hard to write something else, so I try to <u>add</u> something different from myself:<br /> <br /> Black Furies: Motherhood and care<br /> Bone Gnawers: unyielding freedom.<br /> Children of Gaia: hiding the forbidden<br /> Fianna: home<br /> Fenrir: glory to the heroes<br /> Glass Walkers: progress and adaptation to unknown future<br /> Red Talons: vengeance incarnate<br /> Shadow Lords: court of shadows/knife in shadow/ couirt of knives<br /> Silent Striders: death walkers<br /> Silver Fangs: rotten nobility<br /> Stargazers: balance.<br /> Older Brother: hidden secrets<br /> Younger Brother: regretting irreversible<br /> <br /> Black Spiral Dancers: evil has no boundaries<br /> Ronin: rejection of community\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T03:14:47-07:00","id":1512705,"title":"","content":"Neat idea! Will be cool to see how one see the Tribes at the core!<br /> <br /> <b>Black Furies: </b>A militant misandrist Amazon Brigade wit ha Berserk Button of Men's violence against women and children<br /> <b>Bone Gnawers:</b> Urban werewolves who choose to be homeless and adhere to democratic ideals as they do not see themselves superior to others.<br /> <b>Children of Gaia:</b> The most egalitarian of the tribes who see themselves as peacekeepers and mediators with a mild Church Militant streak<br /> <b>Fianna: </b>Celtic Garou with significant ties to the Fair Folk and tendencies of hedonism, eg. they love partying, music, drinking, and lovemaking thus the biggest Hypocrites when it comes to Metis cubs...<br /> <b>Get of Fenris: </b>Nordic Proud Warrior Race Guys with personal berserk button<br /> <b>Glass Walkers:</b> Urban werewolves, everything the Bone Gnawlers are not<br /> <b>Red Talons: </b>A savage militantly misanthropic wolves-only tribe<br /> <b>Shadow Lords: </b>European nobility with less-than-scrupulous methods. Seconds-in-command to the Silver Fangs, with Starscream tendencies to usurp them and become the new rulers of the entire Garou Nation.<br /> <b>Silent Striders:</b> Traveler, messenger and necromancer Jackal shifters who survived because nobody noticed they are not wolves<br /> <b>Silver Fangs: </b>The traditional ruling tribe with porud past and endemic mental illness<br /> <b>Stargazers: </b>Ascetic monks and astrologers from the Far East<br /> <b>Uktena: </b>Magical Native Americans who delve for new secrets... sometimes from dubious sources.<br /> <b>Wendigo:</b> Native American Proud Warrior Race Guys with a dim view of non-Natives<br /> <br /> <b>Black Spiral Dancers: </b>They\u2019re a whole tribe of sociopathic, bloodthirsty lunatics with a desire to sow chaos and destruction for their own sake.They are the embodiment of Equal-Opportunity Evil, they accept Garou from all over the world. Race, gender, and breed are no object, unlike some of the Gaia Garou tribes...\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T05:26:38-07:00","id":1512713,"title":"","content":"BF- Misandrists<br /> BG- Poor<br /> CoG-Compromise<br /> Fia- Virility cult<br /> GoF-Warrior cult<br /> GW- Rich<br /> RT-Misanthropes<br /> SL-magnificent bastards<br /> SS-cryptic messengers and cthonic explorers<br /> SF-Aristocrats<br /> SG-Ascetics<br /> Ukt- sketchy<br /> Wen- survival cult.<br /> <br /> Every tribe has points worth praising and condemning.<br /> <br /> <br /> For example, the CoG are welcoming of all-sorts of people, but that gives them a weaker tribal identity and less cohesion and history shows that when you don't have traditions some people have a strong tendency to make weird ones. They like diplomacy and that means they've murdered less people who shouldn't have been murdered, but that just slows things down and gets in the way sometimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T06:09:30-07:00","id":1512716,"title":"","content":"Good summaries, but it's not really a reboot, what would you change in order to be a rebbot? Would any policy have to change, would there be a change in any custom of the tribes, if so, which one? Would others form? New Factions? New Antagonists? New shapeshifting races to alter the balance of strength? Perhaps, new tribes. A tribe made up of Ronin or maybe one made up of Metis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T06:34:12-07:00","id":1512718,"title":"","content":"If there would be a reboot, but would be the same Werewolf: the Apocalypse?<br /> I think I would only change one or two thing<br /> <br /> One, would make the Garou smart and less like a cult - they are (were) like Harry Potter's wizards; lived a shaltered, totally out of touch with the world life to the point they were unable to properly work in a society or blend in<br /> The shifters should be the blend of the physical and spiritual, flesh and spirit, and their case, Human and Wolf - so they should live among Humans and know the world, to &quot;feel&quot; what it became, because Humanity and Weaver/Wyrm - and not becasue they are linked to Gaia to force them<br /> After the First Change go to Garou bootcamp and be trained, but still remain part of the human/wolf society and the personal horror elements should be the juggling with your human life, school, work with the duties toward Gaiai and the spirits and the fact, the world became Hell, and your people were part of it and partially responsible to the current situation<br /> <br /> Would ditch the War of Rages and would lose the Garou superior status. They would be just one of the Shifters. - it makes 0 sense, after what they have done with the other races (and each other) Gaia and the Spriit wolrd not turned their collective back on the bloodthirsty maniacs and consider them servants of the Wyrm<br /> <br /> The main enemy would be Weaver, not Wyrm and would be a heavy focus to help Wyrm to escape and heal to became the Dragon of Balance again to fix things<br /> <br /> Lastly, would lose the almighty Gaia worldview - like how many shifter races did already<br /> Order, Chaos, Balance between the two... these ae universal things, and what happens in a dust called Gaiai in the far corner in the universe simply do not matter. And the fact the Universe is still working kind of proves this worldview...<br /> The Bastet &quot;cosmology&quot; the best in this case, Chalash and Asura are seperate things, Asura is the creation of Chalash, true, but a troublemaker in its own right, something... &quot;small&quot;. Giaia is the Planet. Improtant but not unviersal, something the characters could associate abd deal with, could achieve something fighting against Asura and its creations and make the world better.<br /> Or the Rokea one... the creations of Qyrll wandered to the dry land and made the Dry Land so scared, made a bunch of shifters, nothing cosmic or universal... just local.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 05-25-2023, 09:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T06:43:09-07:00","id":1512720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1512718#post1512718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there would be a reboot, but would be the same Werewolf: the Apocalyps?<br /> I think I would only change one or two thing<br /> One, would make the Garou smart and less like a cult - they are (were) like Harry Potter's wizard; lived a shaltered, totally out of touch with the world life to the point they were unable to properly work in a society or blend in<br /> The shifter should be the blend of the physical and spiritual, flesh and spirit, and their case, Human and Wolf - so they should live among Humans and know the world, to &quot;feel&quot; what it became, because Humanity and Weaver/Wyrm. - and not becasue they are linked to Gaia to force them After the First Change go to Garou bootcamp and be trained, but still remain part of the human/wolf society and the personal horror elements should be the juggling with your human life, school, work with the duties toward Gaiai and the spirits and the fact, the world became Hell, and your people were part of it and partially responsible to the current situation<br /> Would ditch the War of Rages and would lose the Garou superior status. They would be just one of the Shifters. - it makes 0 sense, after what they have done with the other races (and each other) Gaia and the Spriit wolrd not turned their collective back on the bloodthirsty maniacs and consider them servants of the Wyrm<br /> The main enemy would be Weaver, not Wyrm and would be a heavy focus to help Wyrm to escape and heal to became the Dragon of Balance again to fix tings<br /> Lastly, would lose the almighty Giai worldview - like how many shifter races did already<br /> Order, Chaos, Balance between the two... these ae universal things, and what happens in a dust called Gaiai in the far corner in the universe simply do not matter. And the fact the Universe is still working kind of proves this worldview...<br /> The Bastet &quot;cosmology&quot; the best in this case, Chalash and Asura are seperate things, Asura is the creation of Chalash, true, but a troublemaker in its own right, something... Giaia is the -planet, &quot;small&quot; , improtant but not unviersal, something the characters could deal with, could achieve something fighting against Asura and its creations<br /> Or the Rokea one... the creations of Qyrll wandered to the dry land and made the Dry Land so scared, made a bunch of shifters, nothing cosmic or universal... just local.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a bad idea, however I wouldn't dismiss the idea of Gaia as a universal concept completely, I mean, I think some tribes believe in it while others have this less embellished view of Gaia would be more interesting, it creates friction and gives one more reason tribes are not a single entity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T06:44:00-07:00","id":1512721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1512716#post1512716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good summaries, but it's not really a reboot, what would you change in order to be a rebbot? Would any policy have to change, would there be a change in any custom of the tribes, if so, which one? Would others form? New Factions? New Antagonists? New shapeshifting races to alter the balance of strength? Perhaps, new tribes. A tribe made up of Ronin or maybe one made up of Metis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, since they ARE using the tribe names for most and since some aspects of the old are kept, I feel the reboot's focus should be on making the tribes something that new players would want to play with no prior knowledge. Especially in cases like Red Talons or lupus, both are made into these massive hurdles to play in the fanbase when they really don't require that.<br /> <br /> To offer an example of what I mean, the Red Talons have often been seen as unplayable and near impossible to play well in a larger game (pbp, chat,etc.) Despite the common stereotype of the Red Talons as the 'wolf tribe', that isn't actually the core of the tribe. Any lupus from a non-GW non-Gnawer tribe can be a feral woods liver. Instead, Red Talons are strongly defined by their willing denial and forced ignorance. Unlike the Glass Walkers who are human-focused mostly because humanity fascinates them over choosing to be less wolf, Red Talons are willingly choosing to deny any humanity in themselves and exist as true wolves.<br /> <br /> But like there is no 'True Scotchman', there is no one way a wolf can be. A wolf does not consider itself on how it SHOULD act or what is proper behaviour for wolves. For every family-pack, there are the large communities in Yellowstone with MULTIPLE breeding females. As well, atavism is not something unknown to humans. There are plenty of people who choose to give up on the trappings of civilization. What the Red Talons look for is a stereotype.<br /> <br /> One that they themselves cannot live by, as a tribe is not a pack. Red Talons have writing, they have specific rites and even their own takes which laws of the Litany are valid. They have as much human culture as any other tribe, they just deny it.<br /> <br /> Hence, Denial and Call for Ignorance. When playing a Talon, you are playing someone who has been taught to see any other way of living as sinful and wrong and something they MUST deny in themselves. They must live a life of simple action and thought, for overthinking is Wrong.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 05-25-2023, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T06:52:20-07:00","id":1512722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1512721#post1512721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, since they ARE using the tribe names for most and since some aspects of the old are kept, I feel the reboot's focus should be on making the tribes something that new players would want to play with no prior knowledge. Especially in cases like Red Talons or lupus, both are made into these massive hurdles to play in the fanbase when they really don't require that.<br /> <br /> To offer an example of what I mean, the Red Talons have often been seen as unplayable and near impossible to play well in a larger game (pbp, chat,etc.) Despite the common stereotype of the Red Talons as the 'wolf tribe', that isn't actually the core of the tribe. Any lupus from a non-GW non-Gnawer tribe can be a feral woods liver. Instead, Red Talons are strongly defined by their willing denial and forced ignorance. Unlike the Glass Walkers who are human-focused mostly because humanity fascinates them over choosing to be less wolf, Red Talons are willingly choosing to deny any humanity in themselves and exist as true wolves.<br /> <br /> But like there is no 'True Scotchman', there is no one way a wolf can be. A wolf does not consider itself on how it SHOULD act or what is proper behaviour for wolves. For every family-pack, there are the large communities in Yellowstone with MULTIPLE breeding females. What the Red Talons look for is a stereotype. As well, atavism is not something unknown to humans. There are plenty of people who choose to give up on the trappings of civilization.<br /> <br /> One that they themselves cannot live by, as a tribe is not a pack. Red Talons have writing, they have specific rites and even their own takes which laws of the Litany are valid. They have as much human culture as any other tribe, they just deny it.<br /> <br /> Hence, Denial and Call for Ignorance. When playing a Talon, you are playing someone who has been taught to see any other way of living as sinful and wrong and something they MUST deny in themselves. They must live a life of simple action and thought, for overthinking is Wrong.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You have a good point, but this alone isn't enough for a rebbot, this could be only a Rewrite of the first editions updated for these years. Isn't bad, but I can't call it a rebbot, I guess you also need new things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T07:09:09-07:00","id":1512724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1512722#post1512722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You have a good point, but this alone isn't enough for a rebbot, this could be only a Rewrite of the first editions updated for these years. Isn't bad, but I can't call it a rebbot, I guess you also need new things.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, a reboot is not really defined by changing too much. A reboot is resetting things and then finding a way to do something differently. For example TMNT has done the same story over 10 different ways, just experimenting with each aspect of the story in different iterations.<br /> <br /> So for this hypothetical W5, since the focus seems to be to allow more freedom of expression for the players with none of the Nation bearing down upon them, the Nation exists in a way. But a huge part of the change is that they won the war of Apocalypse or at least they SAY they did. The closeness of the Apocalypse time is no longer and tribes are back to being on each other's back. The 'apocalypse' of the title is now the slow decline of the nation as a whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T07:35:27-07:00","id":1512728,"title":"","content":"Worse than that makes sense, a plot of several tribes that should come together to face a common enemy, but are too busy trying to rip each other's heads off for advantage and even supremacy, that even makes sense and more could be added with supplements, although this could still work in older editions, this idea still has potential. Anyway, how do you imagine the Garou nation would look in this context?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T07:37:46-07:00","id":1512729,"title":"","content":"What the Legacy books showed to me about the core aspects of the tribes in a few words for each and could be straight up applied to a true continuation, a true W5 for me:<br /> <br /> <b>Black Furies:</b> Worship the Wyld and the feminine aspect of spirituality for they have many secrets, avenge the vulnerable;<br /> <b>Bone Gnawers: </b>We have a strong sense of community towards the marginalized and fighting for their improvement;<br /> <b>Children of Gaia: </b>Harmonize the differences among such different peoples, to unify them and learn to live with the differences;<br /> <b>Fianna: </b>Love the land your live in, love your family, enjoy life for it can be short and remember where you came from;<br /> <b>Get of Fenris:</b> Sacrifice yourself to stem the Wyrmtide, be adamant against the challenges presented and build a strong family to fight alongside you, whatever it takes;<br /> <b>Glass Walkers:</b> Humanity's tools and their spirituality can be the solution to win the Apocalypse War, learn how to use them and improve upon them, adapt them;<br /> <b>Red Talons:</b> Humans act like all planet is theirs. They're just another animal and must be reminded to be just that, protect against their hunger and killing spree;<br /> <b>Shadow Lords:</b> The ends justify the means, the fight for Gaia demands an iron fist. Ruthlessness must be tempered by cunning, wisdom and honor though;<br /> <b>Silent Striders:</b> We lost our homeland and now we'll help others to avoid such shame, we seek vengeance and our stolen legacy;<br /> <b>Silver Fangs:</b> Nobility of the blood was earned by our ancestors long ago, some indulge in it, others honor it. Tradition has its power, but it must be tempered with valor;<br /> <b>Stargazers:</b> To balance Rage and Reason is the key for breaking the Weaver's webs and cleanse the Wyrm's poison, but balance has a multitude of ways to be expressed;<br /> <b>Uktena:</b> The Wyrm's secrets are key for his defeat, those are the most dangerous and precious mysteries. Other mysteries are also important no wisdom can be dismissed;<br /> <b>Wendigo: </b>Cold and rageful as the blizzard, pure as the fresh snow and bitter against those who wronged us. We keep to the old ways Gaia taught us, thriving where many would perish.<br /> <br /> <b>Black Spiral Dancers:</b> Gaia is mad, letting such degenerate state of the world draws itself on and on, we must make it quick. Kill Gaia. Don't let this b**** torture us any longer, torture her back just for Her to see what's like to suffer in Her hands!<br /> <br /> <b>Ronin:</b> All tribes are mad in their own ways, I must deal with the problem and the spirits in my own way. I don't have a Patron to guide me so I must make every action count.<br /> <br /> <b>Skin Dancers: </b>Some of us realize what the Garou meant when they said we could never understand and try to do things on our own terms, some of us want to take revenge against those Garou who wronged us and some are straight up mad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1876-fenixpp","name":"Fenixpp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T08:34:58-07:00","id":1512740,"title":"","content":"Garou are tragic heroes. They are strong and often very charming and clever, but they are proud, flawed,, and often get screwed over by beings beyond their understanding. Vampires are figures grounded in reality and almost solely obsessed with the material world and their own internal struggles, but Garou take on a more mythical aspect as they enter strange lands and overcome manifestations of abstract concepts. <br /> Like Greek heroes, there's a strong sense of heritage and sequence: Perseus is some kind of grandfather to Heracles, Odysseus recalls Heracles actions in troy.. so to do werewolves obsess over having some amazing grandfather or marrying the son of an elder she-wolf who did X feat or looking exactly like their famous uncle or having a fetished passed down through nine generations of the family. <br /> <br /> <br /> at the same time the tribes need to have a lot of compares and contrasts to one another. The RT reject humanity; the GW reject the wolf. The GW are rich, the BG poor. The stargazers reject worldly desire, the Fianna are all about it. The CoG are welcoming and tolerant, the GoF tell applicants to harden the fuck up and stop being such a pussy. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think the Wendigo don't really have anything to say that another tribe doesn't do better. That's probably the biggest outlier. <br /> I think it's weird there's only one evil tribe. Garou are very flawed figures: There's room for more. <br /> <br /> and I think the lack of African tribes is something to be remedied. Ditto with things like south east Asia and Australia having nothing serious despite canid populations. Perhaps we could look at the Hakken and apply the concept elsewhere: Like say there's a tribe of werewolves in Africa that follow Antelope and despite obvious ethnic differences and a few cultural aspects the character of the tribe is the same as those who follow Stag and the spirits Stag and Antelope have connections so they're considered the same, at least externally and from a rules perspective. Brother tribes perhaps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T08:47:26-07:00","id":1512742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1512740#post1512740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Wendigo don't really have anything to say that another tribe doesn't do better. That's probably the biggest outlier.<br /> I think it's weird there's only one evil tribe. Garou are very flawed figures: There's room for more.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that every tribe has extremists that can be considered &quot;evil&quot; and you can even add more if you're creative, I like to call them heretic packs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T13:02:32-07:00","id":1512764,"title":"","content":"I do think that it\u2019s useful to have an image of the archetypes in your mind and so I\u2019ll share some of my own off the top of my head, both to help me clarify them and to participate in this.<br /> <br /> <b>Black Furies - </b>Warriors of the Feminine Spirit | The Avengers of the victims of the Patriarch (Womenkind, Children, The Wilds; certain culturally relevant categories of men and others depending on camp) &amp; Guardians of the Sacred Wilderness &amp; Primordial Taboos; associated imo with the \u2018barbarian\u2019 fringes and mysteries of the Hellenic World such as the Scythians, Cretan, Sicilian, &amp; Eleusian Mystery Cults, Amazons, etc.<br /> <i>(in my opinion an under-utilized quality of the Black Furies comes from their association with the Hellenic \u2018Furies\u2019; they are tied to primordial-vengeance spirits and so when those primeval taboos are broken such as the patriarchal domination of the feminine, matricide, kinslaying, violation of sacred places, etc. they rise to avenge those violations)</i><br /> <br /> <b>Bone Gnawers - </b>The Outcast Wolves | The Bone Gnawers are the survivors and the flotsam of Garou History; the Omegas, Garou-Born, Cowards, Dishonored, and Bastards of the Nation were driven from their ancestral septs and those who struggled to survive would be brought together by Rat, Jackal, Hyena, Coyote, Crow, and the other Scavenger spirits | While Bone Gnawers would later be invoked by other parts of the Nation and compromises be made the Bone Gnawers would settle into agnostic camps for survival; the best of them becoming champions of the downtrodden and the forgotten places, haunting them alongside the scavengers and spirits of \u2018low cunning\u2019<br /> <i>(I view a central conflict of the Bone Gnawers being between those elders who have managed to piece together an ideology under Rat and the Ronin &amp; Lone Wolves on the other end who have not technically received even Rat\u2019s blessing. Most Bone Gnawers sit somewhere in the middle; minding-their-own, working for others at some price, and primarily fighting when their own trod out turfs are disturbed by invasion/taint)</i><br /> <br /> <b>Children of Gaia - </b>The (self-appointed) Vanguard of the Sacred Mother | The Children of Gaia are bound by a vision of sacred unity and harmony which is all-inclusive (man, beast, Garou, spirit, etc.); they seek to bring about a restoration of that sacred and primordial state by whatever means available to them | that does mean that some of them are the hippie peaceniks of legend whereas others are as much a self-appointed leadership tribe as the Silver Fangs or Shadow Lords and others try as much as the Glass Walkers, Red Talons, or what have you to integrate themselves with the world of men, beasts, spirits, etc.<br /> <i>(A good way of differentiating the Children of Gaia and Bone Gnawers is this in my mind: the Bone-Gnawers would accept a Garou-Born because they are outcasts and proven survivors on the fringes of the Nation, the Children of Gaia would accept a Garou-Born because their must be a place for them in the Mother\u2019s Body and if the Garou-Born is able to foster their own vision of unity; the Children of Gaia do have their own Pure Breed from Unicorn but will accept other Garou because they are dedicated to a vision of a world without tribe - although whether that means a single tribe under Unicorn, Wolf, or Gaia is a matter of debate)</i><br /> <br /> <b>Fianna - </b>The Warriors of Stag represent Wild Virility, Passion, Fertility, Family, &amp; Pride (What they would call the Great Song of Life) | The Fianna are defined by the sacred passions of life which for them became inevitably tied with what their human kin were doing - which is how traditions of oral legend and crafting and cooking become part of their oeuvre; their ties with the Fair Folk come from this same great wellspring of Life and Passion which drives the Fae | The Fianna are associated with the Celtic tradition but their general quality is one defined by Stag, Passion, Life (Fertility, Romance, Singing/Dancing, Fighting, Family, Jealousy, Rivalry, Pride, Eating/Drinking, Screwing, Hospitality, etc.)<br /> <br /> <b>Get of Fenris - </b>The War Cult amongst A Cult of Warriors | The Get of Fenris are united by a hardened dedication to the Death-Wolf/War-Wolf tradition above all (and they may honestly resemble the original Garou the most) | The Fenrir are the Koryos Warrior-Wolf Cults; chewing psychoactive roots, entering battle frenzies, willing to use whatever tactics might be necessary to harass and kill their targets, and in many ways living outside of traditional life and community | The Fenrir have ties to Scandinavian traditions but like the Black Furies (and Fiannia to a lesser extent) they represent a primordial and monstrous nature-loving association which the groups of humans who wrote things down associated with malevolent outsiders (giants, mystery cults, warrior dead, monster wolves, etc.)<br /> <i>(Here\u2019s how I would distinguish the Fianna &amp; Fenrir, who are something of a complimentary pair | The Fianna are Garou who live inside the camp - heavily involved with their kin, heavily involved with human (and wolf) life, heavily invested in the community festivities and the rhythms of living in the Song of Stag | The Fenrir are Garou who live outside the camp - their kinfolk maintain regular life semi-independently with semi-regular visits from the garou element, the Fenrir live amongst themselves in a perpetual war-camp, deeply invested in the secret mysteries of the Death-Wolf and ever-striving to prove themselves in the blood of their tribal enemies)</i><br /> <br /> <b>Glass Walkers - </b>The Friends of (so-called) Civilization | These Garou were the first to be impressed by the gifts of the Weaver to humanity and unlike the other tribes saw those powers and those secrets as the future, leaving them to abandon the old ways in favor of the ones which came alongside humanity, society, and the Weaver - so long as these tools could ostensibly be used in favor of the Mother and they kept closer to the hum of human life than the cold embrace of the Weaver<br /> <i>(In the same but opposite way that the Red Talons are liable to fall to Triatic taint, the Glass Walkers are. They left behind the old ways in favor of the sacred rites developed in communion in human society and the Weaver. The Glass Walkers who remain closest to Gaia are the ones who best connect humanity\u2019s gifts to their primal roots in the human spirit, the ones who stray are those who are drawn from humanity and towards the mechanical dance of the Weaver)</i><br /> <br /> <b>Red Talons - </b>The Friends of the Wolves | Whereas the Glass Walkers moved towards humanity after their contact with the Weaver, the Red Talons ran away and have been running ever since | The Red Talons have to various degrees excised the primordial human elements of the dual-nature, remaining dedicated to all the aspects of Wolf and the Old Wilderness instead, harkening themselves towards the Wilds-That-Was prior to the Fall of the Weaver<br /> <i>(On the other side of the coin from the Glass Walkers; the Red Talons closest to Gaia are those who combine their concern for the Wilds with a Paleolithic Human-sensibility, those who stray towards fall into the Wyld\u2019s grasp are those who increasingly abandon the human-spirit and even aspects of the wolf-spirit which are too like the man-spirit in favor of the primeval wilderness and naturalist chaos of the Wyld)</i><br /> <br /> <b>Shadow Lords - </b>The Cruel Necessities of Grand-Father | The Shadow Lords are those who have embraced the unpleasant pragmatism which assists them in their goals and desire to succeed - intrigue, poison, culling, assassination, subtlety, and deception are all parts of the unsavory implements that have always been known but had to be practiced out of sight | The Shadow Lords would also recognize the useful elements of humanity - those patriarchs that the Black Furies loathed for the breaking of taboos were undeniably able to accrue immense resources and influence; the Shadow Lords asked how that might be put to use in service of Gaia and so they would embrace the human innovations in authority and organization | The Shadow Lords are looked at with wary suspicion by other Garou - but as long as they defeat their enemies, serve the strong loyally, and root out the Wyrm, what is to be done?<br /> <i>(The Shadow Lords were the appointed \u2018enemy within\u2019 of early werewolf, even having a section of their first tribe book dedicate to villainy; I think that alone is too one-dimensional but I do feel it\u2019s an important element. Any tribe can be villainous for a session or a chronicle but the Shadow Lords are the tribe every other tribe would imagine as the most-likely villains. At their best the Shadow Lords live up to their own BS - they really are using the tools of the Patriarch, Intrigue, &amp; Cruelty in service of the more-honorable leaders and Gaia. At their worst they really are planning to use those methods to raise themselves to power, even if the honorable-leaders are competent to rule. Whether at their best or worst however the Shadow Lords are prepared to arrange for the demise of any leaders who prove too weak to uphold their duties; they are the cult who kills the golden king so that the golden king might live)</i><br /> <br /> <b>Silent Striders - </b>Keepers of Dead Mysteries | Outcasts, Secret-Keepers, Loners, Wanderers, &amp; Emissaries to the Dead &amp; the Shadow | The Silent Striders serve as the nerve tissue connecting disparate septs and caerns while also being an early warning network for whatever goes on in the dark places in-between septs | They are keepers of ancient secrets and mysteries as well, such as the roads to the Underworld and the cold voices of the dead | They are outcasts like the Bone Gnawers or Lone Wolves but unlike them have remained dedicated to their Sacred Mysteries (those who don\u2019t will become Bone Gnawers or Ronin in time, which may explain part of the psychological reason for the Striders loathing of those groups)<br /> <i>(I view the presence of Cthonic cults as being an important part of Garou in general, if one that doesn\u2019t get talked about openly or very often. Every tribe probably has their own version and various degrees of stress placed upon it - but the Silent Striders and Older Brother probably have it the most | I view the differences between Older Brother as being fairly nuanced; Older Brother has mysteries connected with living and active traditions albeit the Apocalypse and is still engaged in the upkeep of them; the Silent Striders are the remnants of Post-Apocalyptic mysteries that are largely dead but for the relics they still carry, but dead does not mean they are without power)</i><br /> <br /> <b>Silver Fangs - </b>The Sacred Nobility | The Silver Fangs somehow gained the primordial blessing of nobility (kingship, queenship, etc.) in ancient times - there should probably be several contradictory reasons why but it\u2019s important that this claim has some veracity to it | The Core Problem of the Silver Fangs comes from trying to figure out what Sacred Kingship means, in practice, 10,000+ years after the first Queen received the blessings of Sun, Moon, Wolf, Mother, Death, Falcon, etc. The Silver Fangs are torn apart by their own contradictory existence and all the neuroses that comes with it. At their best, when some Silver Fang king figures out his own BS, they can truly act as living-heroes who inspire, invigorate, and lead the Garou of today with confidence and success. At their worst when some Silver Fang queen is unable to parse her own BS, they become parodies of themselves, the best of these being drooling idiots and pitiable and the worst being terrifying and horrible maniacs. <br /> <br /> <b>Stargazers - </b>The Dreaming Wolves | These Garou are highly sensitive to the precarious nature of existence and from the first moments of sapience have felt the need to understand the mysteries which define them and uphold the metaphysics of their being | the best of these wolves are those who plunge into the psycho sphere and return with useful and actionable insight both into practical existence for the Garou and the metaphysical stakes of their battle, the worst of them are trapped in the endless spiral of their own quixotic selves and are unable to pierce beyond the fetters of their own Egos and come to any fruitful kernels of Wisdom<br /> <i>(Having the Stargazers being the main or central tribe of all of Asia is ridiculous imo, but that\u2019s a can of worms for another day. It makes thematic sense for them to have links to Nepal and Tibet but that shouldn\u2019t be their only links to the material world)</i><br /> <br /> <b>Older Brother - </b>The Ghost Dancers | (I\u2019m not indigenous so pinch of salt for this group and younger brother, check out stuff that James Sombrano has done); Older Brother is the active tribe most tied with the Mysteries, Secrets, and Occult Worlds that other tribes have links to but do not fully delve into; in the post-Apocalypse of the indigenous world they have adopted a fluid strategy of survival through adaption which is reflected by their general association with the water, both the mercurial flow and the hidden depths<br /> <i>(All tribes have mystical concerns, some more than others, but here\u2019s how I would distinguish the Ghost Dancers from the Silent Striders and Stargazers for example | The Ghost Dancers have maintained an active community and living tribe unlike the fragmented Striders and oft-reclusive Stargazers and furthermore the Ghost Dancers are both concerned with their own Sacred Traditions but also take a mercenary interest in every arcane tradition within reach; meanwhile the Silent Striders maintain close ties to the underworld and their own almost-Lovecraftian dead rites while the Stargazers thrust themselves not only into the mystical deluge of spirit worlds but also into the realms of the Psycho-Sphere, Dreaming Realms, Astral, &amp; Far Realms in search of insight)</i><br /> <br /> <b>Younger Brother - </b>The Gale Stalkers | If Middle Brother and Older Brother were more aligned with Earth &amp; Water than Younger Brother is with Air (with an honorable mention to Fire imo). They are defiantly anti-assimilationist and strive to maintain their lives, heritage, traditions, and peoples without compromise or any restriction but what they themselves choose. They are among the fiercest of warriors because of this and have only been sharpened and further enraged by the Apocalypse they\u2019ve. The fierce battle to survive and persist alongside the ways in which the realities of their traditions persist, regardless of what settlers may think, is also a key factor of this tribe.<br /> <i>(The comics they included in the early tribe books are somewhat hit-or-miss but something I appreciate from Younger Brother\u2019s tribe book comic is the premise that the spiritual concerns that indigenous peoples had did not cease even if they were removed from their lands, taboos and spirits and monsters remained, ones that only those who remembered the traditions like Younger Brother could combat. While this is something I feel should be universal in Werewolf, I do feel it deserves a special mention with relation to Older &amp; Younger Brother. Speaking of the Three Brothers - my view is that Older Brother\u2019s purview was the mystical and the ritual, Middle Brother\u2019s purview was the legal and the traditional, while Younger Brother\u2019s purview was social and the active cycle of life.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T13:31:44-07:00","id":1512765,"title":"","content":"I think it is good to consider that since W5 IS a reboot and tries to make the tribes more general, it is important to focus on giving the core in as few words as possible to the new players.<br /> <br /> My go-to example for the Silver Fangs has always been Game of Thrones. Because the whole point of the series (until the 5th season onwards) is that the nobles are infighting while a much bigger threat is coming. It also helps to give you a sense of the isolation the tribe has towards other tribes. Other tribes are smallfolk, who CARES what THEY think.<br /> <br /> In a similar vein, Silent Striders don't travel because they like it, they travel because they lost their home and they are cursed by ghosts haunting them. So they seek redemption for their mistake and try to get rid of the curse upon them.<br /> <br /> The Fianna are a family, but every family has its black sheep. Every family has branches no one wants to talk about.<br /> <br /> The Fenrir are a tribe of war, yes. But the thing they value is not looks, family lines, ableness or any of that. They aren't Spartans who saw no worth in disability. Instead, they focus on how strong your will to keep going is. To go a bit silly, Monty Python's Black Knight is prime Fenrir material.<br /> <br /> In a lot of ways, the Glass Walkers are seen as the Weaver tribe like the Red Talons are seen as the Wyld tribe. It is due to which side the Triatic Entity chose to pick, rather than the tribe itself. Because GWs are defined by Change, they have literally changed the name of their tribe multiple times. While the Red Talons are defined by their enforced stasis to One True Way of the Wolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T14:31:27-07:00","id":1512773,"title":"","content":"Originally: Femininity/The Feminine Mystery, Survival, Unity, Passion, Strength, Progress, Extinction, Pragmatism, The Quest, Nobility, Puzzles, Secrets, and Pain/Hate, respectively. Now? Dunno. \ud83e\udd37\u200d\u2642\ufe0f<br /> <br /> (In perfect hindsight, I suspect better names for the Uktena and Wendigo would have been Hunters in Darkness and White Howlers, respectively. Not sure what better names for the Croatan or Bunyip would have been.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T14:39:46-07:00","id":1512774,"title":"","content":"The Glass Walker relation to the Weaver is not symmetrical to the Red Talon relationship with the Wyld. The former thought that it was neat and there was vast, unexplored potential to be had in human use of tools and threw themselves into it. The latter take in the lost and abandoned by the world, as a result of their witness to mass extinction, and they do it because no one else makes room for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T16:17:55-07:00","id":1512790,"title":"","content":"Black Furies: Battle priests of womanhood<br /> Bone Gnawers: Wisdom from the gutters<br /> Children of Gaia: To win the war, first you must make friends<br /> Fianna: Warrior poets in it for the stories that will be told<br /> Fenrir: Best of the Best and desperate to prove it<br /> Glass Walkers: Masters of Tools and Human society<br /> Red Talons: Big bad wolves out for blood<br /> Shadow Lords: Amoral pragmatists<br /> Silent Striders: Wandering nightstalkers<br /> Silver Fangs: The Once and Future Kings<br /> Stargazers: Masters of body and spirit<br /> Uktena: cosmopolitan delvers into ancestral mysteries<br /> Wendigo: Righters of wrongs at any cost<br /> <br /> Black Spiral Dancers: A fetid, disgusting mirror of human (and Garou) depravity","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T17:13:54-07:00","id":1512797,"title":"","content":"Personal spin focused on rage (and Rage), W5 or not;<br /> <br /> Black Furies: Rage in place of the vengeful.<br /> <br /> Bone Gnawers: Rage in defence of the downtrodden.<br /> <br /> Children of Gaia: Rage against defilement of purity.<br /> <br /> Wild Hunt (Fianna): Rage until abandon and ecstasy.<br /> <br /> Get of Fenris: Rage against the false gods and their whims.<br /> <br /> Glass Walkers: Rage until innovation breaks through.<br /> <br /> Red Talons: Rage against control and suppression.<br /> <br /> Shadow Lords: Rage put to an end and a purpose.<br /> <br /> Silent Striders: Rage to forget not the homeland and the past.<br /> <br /> Silver Fangs: Rage to inspire the greater good and call to action.<br /> <br /> Stargazers: Rage until emptied of rage to attain clarity of mind.<br /> <br /> River\u2019s Eye (Uktena, Older Brother): Rage against ignorance and concealment.<br /> <br /> Winter\u2019s Mouth (Wendigo, Younger Brother): Rage in defence of the self and selfhood.<br /> <br /> Black Spiral Dancers: Rage in meaningless pain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T08:06:29-07:00","id":1513194,"title":"","content":"There's always a nice spicy hypocrisy to most tribes. The Red Talons, in going against their better nature for dogma, are ironically one of the most human tribes. Black Furies are sexist, Wendigo are racist, Shadow Lords can never be the best leaders because nobody trusts them. Glass walkers are all about change yet they flirt so closely with the embodiment of stasis, Children of Gaia are so liberal that they've made a culture out of it, silver fangs have fucked their genes up in the name of purity... <br /> <br /> ..Except for the GoF and Uktena: those guys are exactly what they want to be without any irony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T08:26:08-07:00","id":1513196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513194#post1513194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's always a nice spicy hypocrisy to most tribes. The Red Talons, in going against their better nature for dogma, are ironically one of the most human tribes. Black Furies are sexist, Wendigo are racist, Shadow Lords can never be the best leaders because nobody trusts them. Glass walkers are all about change yet they flirt so closely with the embodiment of stasis, Children of Gaia are so liberal that they've made a culture out of it, silver fangs have fucked their genes up in the name of purity...<br /> <br /> ..Except for the GoF and Uktena: those guys are exactly what they want to be without any irony.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess the with the Red Talons, the Furies, CoG and the Glass Walkers is one of that cases where you try so hard be something that you become the opposite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T11:35:32-07:00","id":1513215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513194#post1513194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's always a nice spicy hypocrisy to most tribes. The Red Talons, in going against their better nature for dogma, are ironically one of the most human tribes. Black Furies are sexist, Wendigo are racist, Shadow Lords can never be the best leaders because nobody trusts them. Glass walkers are all about change yet they flirt so closely with the embodiment of stasis, Children of Gaia are so liberal that they've made a culture out of it, silver fangs have fucked their genes up in the name of purity...<br /> <br /> ..Except for the GoF and Uktena: those guys are exactly what they want to be without any irony.</div> </div> </div> </div>RE: Little Brother, it's difficult to be racist when you aren't the ones in power, since that typically relies on being able to force others to accede to your wishes and then imposing a system on them. It requires going along with the system in power, which is not really something most of them do. If they did, they wouldn't be struggling and dying. It'd probably be better to focus Little Brother's troubles on other issues with the predicament of their kin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T07:03:49-07:00","id":1513389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513215#post1513215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> RE: Little Brother, it's difficult to be racist when you aren't the ones in power, since that typically relies on being able to force others to accede to your wishes and then imposing a system on them. It requires going along with the system in power, which is not really something most of them do. If they did, they wouldn't be struggling and dying. It'd probably be better to focus Little Brother's troubles on other issues with the predicament of their kin.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> it perfectly matches the way most people sees racism, ie being prejudiced against others based on race.<br /> The wendigo distrust and/or despise anyone who isn't like them. Which, seeing how little native american exists compared to other ethnic groups is not a good position to stand on. And an irrational one, since they reject the tribes that might help them, but which end up abandonning their effort in front of wendigo's hostility toward &quot;wyrmbringers&quot;. Such position will inevitably lead to the wendigo's doom sooner or later.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T07:09:35-07:00","id":1513392,"title":"","content":"With Little Brother it's even more complicated than that. They hold grudges for what was done to them by the Wyrmcomers. And a lot of the Wyrmcomers are not really giving them reasons to trust them or making the effort to cooperate with them. So it's a complicated situation that's bound to explode.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T07:46:27-07:00","id":1513394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513392#post1513392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Little Brother it's even more complicated than that. They hold grudges for what was done to them by the Wyrmcomers. And a lot of the Wyrmcomers are not really giving them reasons to trust them or making the effort to cooperate with them. So it's a complicated situation that's bound to explode.</div> </div> </div> </div>As the Silent Strider tribebook pointed out, they hate the non-native tribes for even being there, they hate the Croatan for dying and leaving them, they hate the Uktena for not staying purely native, and they hate themselves for not dying with the Croatan. Their personal sense of pain and wounded pride runs deep, and will likely be their undoing. (Such was the revised edition run up to the Apocalypse, at least. I've no idea to what degree 5th ed is trying to tell the same story.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T08:00:22-07:00","id":1513396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513392#post1513392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Little Brother it's even more complicated than that. They hold grudges for what was done to them by the Wyrmcomers. And a lot of the Wyrmcomers are not really giving them reasons to trust them or making the effort to cooperate with them. So it's a complicated situation that's bound to explode.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> as no one of consequence mention, it's not merely against europeans.<br /> <br /> If the wendigo were &quot;merely&quot; racists against europeans or european originated american for past issues, it would still be irrational and self defeatinf, but at least it would be comprehensible. But they also distrust non native that aren't part of the wyrmbringers.<br /> <br /> Add to that they're bitter at the uktena for no longuer being full on natives (yeah, apparently uktena are basically &quot;race traitors&quot; for opening themselves to anyone open to their philosophy), and the croatan for the crime of leaving them all alone (I guess mass sacrifice to save the world is not a good enough excuse) and we sees that the wendigo are defined byhatred toward anyone not fitting their very narrow criterias for a trustworthy person.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T08:09:41-07:00","id":1513397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513394#post1513394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> . Their personal sense of pain and wounded pride runs deep, and will likely be their undoing. (Such was the revised edition run up to the Apocalypse, at least. I've no idea to what degree 5th ed is trying to tell the same story.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Although I guess it won't matter to W5, Apocalypse Records, the BJD of Werewolf 20 ends up with a reunion of shadow lords discussing what they discovered about dangerous devellopments amongs other tribes, which matches many tribal falls from the Time of Judgement Apocalypse. And the wendigo are back taking over a nuclear submarine to eliminates the wyrmbringers.<br /> <br /> Which of course they would do. They refuse to accept that they lost their land, they refuse to be conciliant with non natives, both humans and garous, so it was obvious they would go on an ethnic cleansing, and since they are not up for a fight with the other tribes on the continent, they go for mass destruction weapons.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T08:49:45-07:00","id":1513399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513396#post1513396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> and the croatan for the crime of leaving them all alone (I guess mass sacrifice to save the world is not a good enough excuse) </div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, grief is very rarely rational.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T08:54:19-07:00","id":1513401,"title":"","content":"Little Brother really can't be discussed without acknowledging the metatext of the situation, which is that they weren't written at all by indigenous people but are serving as worse fall guys than the Get of Fenris. That's kind of fucked up, to be honest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T09:32:23-07:00","id":1513409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513401#post1513401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Little Brother really can't be discussed without acknowledging the metatext of the situation, which is that they weren't written at all by indigenous people but are serving as worse fall guys than the Get of Fenris. That's kind of fucked up, to be honest.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true, however in Revised they actually mellowed them out a bit and got in some native people to consult, there are all kinds of acknowledgements in the credits, but I'm not sure how much was writing in that. I feel the goal never was to make them bitter untill the end and lashing out in their rage, but in being brought to sensibility.<br /> <br /> A lot of the ideas in Apocalyptic Record don't sit well with me because they ignore a number of positive developments in Revised settings and delegate them to possible futures while generally leaning into some of the darker interpretations of where the Garou were going.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T10:20:09-07:00","id":1513417,"title":"","content":"I will mention that I was acquainted at the time with Jim Kiley, who wrote the fallen tribes chapter for Apocalypse. The fallen tribes chapter were all intended to be nightmare worst case scenarios that Storytellers could use to make whichever Apocalypse version they wanted to do be even more tragic and doom filled. They were all meant to be a group falling to their worst natures and not any sort of likely future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T10:31:47-07:00","id":1513421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513401#post1513401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Little Brother really can't be discussed without acknowledging the metatext of the situation, which is that they weren't written at all by indigenous people but are serving as worse fall guys than the Get of Fenris. That's kind of fucked up, to be honest.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> i don't think this is relevant to their writing on that matter, since the uktena were also not written by native american, but were far more diverse in their ideologies and far less obsessed with setting past grievances, with only a single camp dedicated to that, a camp which is the uktena &quot;evil camp&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> The problem of the wendigo is not the cultural origin of the writters, but that they are written with an ideology that put them in the &quot;factions that are capital W Wrong&quot; category alongside the red talons and in some ways the black furies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T10:54:20-07:00","id":1513424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513399#post1513399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unfortunately, grief is very rarely rational.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but like a few hundred years passed. grief isn't that multi-generational. IDK to me the Wendigo seem written like some antagonistic tribe that should've either been wiped or conceded and assimilated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T11:28:16-07:00","id":1513428,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m sympathetic to Younger Brother and I think that their inclusion is important, with the comparison to the Black Furies being significant.<br /> <br /> For one thing, albeit it can be easy to forget, Werewolf was originally written as a pro-environmentalist polemic and in that context it would be a mistake to not include prominent indigenous representation, given how many environmental struggles across the globe have indigenous groups as central movers and shakers.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, while Werewolf in theory is a global work, it\u2019s always been focused on the United States in particular and if you\u2019re telling stories about a struggle against the most destructive elements of society and being haunted by the horrors of the past, whose effects linger to this day, again you can\u2019t really not talk about the native experience.<br /> <br /> I think core conflict inherent to Werewolf storytelling is the problem of violence. On one level - anger (and violence) can be experienced as emancipatory. This shows both in irl conflicts where justified anger serves as a powerful motivation (slave revolts, Black Union soldiers in the U.S. Civil War, etc.) but that righteous anger is a highly popular power-fantasy and one which Werewolf has never shied from acknowledging as a key aspect of its appeal (I recall advice in a storytellers guide somewhere that if you and your group all have experience working at McDonalds or Burger King than you should consider running a session or chronicle focused on tearing apart O\u2019Tooleys). There are also very real cases where we (barring the absolute pacifists among us) can imagine violence being necessary to achieve a righteous end. So on one level we have violence and anger both as potentially righteous and useful as well as prime storytelling fodder.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, a core issue of the problem of anger and violence, is that they have limits. They\u2019re both incredibly powerful but they\u2019re not a one-size-fits-all solution to every problem, they can be internally corrosive, and they can be taken to excess and exasperate existing problems or create new ones. Werewolf dwells on this by pointing out the damage that can be caused, both internal and external, but also pointing out how violence and retribution alone is not enough. Even if one could muster the strength for one great knock-out blow against the structure of one\u2019s opposition, there would still be the question of what is to be done in the aftermath. Furthermore in most actual instances of resistance there is no one great knock-out blow or final confrontation, there is a protracted series of confrontations where one must simultaneously strike one\u2019s enemies and build up one\u2019s own community, relationships and forces into something distinct from the old social order.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think it\u2019s fair to expect either players, writers, or storytellers to have a perfect answer to the problem of violence that fits every situation. It\u2019s something that humans have manifestly struggled with for centuries and probably for as long as we\u2019ve been recognizably sentient/sapient.<br /> <br /> I think that Younger Brother plays an important role with regards to the above as the Black Furies in that it both speaks real issues (the settler state in the former case, the patriarchy in the latter case) where righteous anger can support justified resistance as well as being fodder for an outlet of energy in a werewolf game. Both tribes can have flawed elements which acknowledge the real dangers of excess and the flaws of the Nation, but blowing up these flaws so that they smother the core of what made them appealing for play in the first place would be a mistake imo.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m reminded of something that James Sombrano talked about on a podcast, I believe with the Mage the Ascension podcast but it may have been with the Werewolf the Apocalypse podcast. He talked about growing up native and his complex feelings for Older Brother and Younger Brother, and how he felt that both reflected something he felt strongly about and important themes/strains of thought in indigenous movements: the question of assimilationism on the one hand (Older Brother) and the value of community with other oppressed nations and adaption but also the matter of resistance (Younger Brother) and the refusal to allow traditions and customs and sacred relationships to be profaned or destroyed or lost as well as the power of righteous anger and the importance of connection with that anger. He told a story about a LARP he participated in with a large indigenous player membership and how Werewolf was used as a vehicle to explore these ideas and themes, all happening in the irl backdrop of the recent Standing Rock protests and the continued suppression of the settler-state.<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t describe it as well as him or those who were involved, but hearing those stories is one of the reasons why I\u2019m resistant to painting Younger Brother in particular with too cynical or dark a brush or with writing off the importance of the stories and themes which Younger Brother can bring to the game which other setting elements cannot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11637,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","user":"Gryffon15","date":". 05-31-2023, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T12:11:14-07:00","id":1513432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513428#post1513428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m sympathetic to Younger Brother and I think that their inclusion is important, with the comparison to the Black Furies being significant.<br /> <br /> For one thing, albeit it can be easy to forget, Werewolf was originally written as a pro-environmentalist polemic and in that context it would be a mistake to not include prominent indigenous representation, given how many environmental struggles across the globe have indigenous groups as central movers and shakers.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically, and I don't know if it was a deliberate move from the various authors of the gameline, werewolf's tribes can be seen as reflecting various activist/political ideologies and behavior, and most of them are defined by the worse flaws and extremisms of these activist/political ideologies.<br /> <br /> The black furies are the feminists and are fundamentally (and violently) misandrists.<br /> <br /> The red talons are the &quot;humanity is a cancer on the planet&quot; misanthropes. Which is a flaw in itself.<br /> <br /> The glass walker are the tech bros hoping that technology will resolve all issues but mostly blind to their own disconnect from others.<br /> <br /> The \u00e7hildren of gaia are the &quot;peace and love&quot; universalists so trapped in their moral purity act that they rebuke those they want to convince.<br /> <br /> The bone gnawers are the pro poor people activists who never actually help said poor people escape from poverty.<br /> <br /> The get of fenris are the &quot;action first&quot; ones who fails to see any non violent solution to problems.<br /> <br /> The stargazers are the philosophers/deep thinkers trapped in their own minds making them unable to do anything but navel gaze.<br /> <br /> The silver fangs are obviously the royalists and &quot;strong leadership is what will save us&quot; people who fail to go beyond the issues of monarchy.<br /> <br /> The shadow lords are of course the &quot;end justify all means&quot; activists which ends up doing terrible things for their cause and making others distrust them.<br /> <br /> <br /> And following that, the wendigo are the pro native activists, or more specifically, the &quot;natives pro natives&quot;activists, denigrating people who might help them on the basis that they're not natives themselves.<br /> <br /> And I don't know where the fianna and silent striders end up on the &quot;garou tribes are activists&quot; models. Maybe the fianna could be pro irish independance activists, but I have no clue for silent striders.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T12:53:50-07:00","id":1513443,"title":"","content":"In that vein, if I had to guess:<br /> <br /> \u2022The Fianna are pretty clearly influenced by the perception of The Troubles in Ireland and Britain from a Yankee perspective, with the odd voyeurism for the Troubles in particular being a sort of cultural snapshot of a period of time within which Werewolf was written. In retrospect it\u2019s kind of fascinating how many sympathetic characters in Yankee media from the 1970s into the 2000s are former (or active) Irish Republican Army and related groups, I don\u2019t think it really fizzled until the upswing of the War on Terror and having a good decade or so since the last major flare up. (I always recall the main female lead on \u2018Burn Notice\u2019 being former IRA - and naturally an explosives expert). <br /> <br /> \u2022The Silent Striders I\u2019m not so sure about. I feel that they\u2019re definitely influenced by the cultural fascination with the Romani and other \u2018Traveler\u2019 peoples, with the Egypt connection being a natural fascination for a group of goths and wiccans who were already predisposed to be fascinated by the legend of Egyptian mystery and magic (and the traditional connection made between the Romani and Egypt by European chroniclers - for instance the idea of Tarot being drawn from Hermetic concepts drawn from Hermes Thrice-Great in ancient Egypt as well as being associated with the Romani). In retrospect however, in a post-Iraq War world, the comparison of Silent Striders with middle eastern refugees feels natural - albeit a matter to be handled delicately, if one doesn\u2019t opt to ignore it entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T13:12:23-07:00","id":1513446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513424#post1513424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but like a few hundred years passed. grief isn't that multi-generational. IDK to me the Wendigo seem written like some antagonistic tribe that should've either been wiped <b>or conceded and assimilated.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>This? This right here? This is the problem. People are quick to find fault with YB, but fail to realize that the Euro-Americans are often being really, really unreasonable and putting up an &quot;our way or else&quot; system that &quot;just happens&quot; to have bad to lethal results for people who live in other ways.<br /> <br /> Yeah, sure it &quot;just happens&quot; to. Look who made it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T15:44:46-07:00","id":1513468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513446#post1513446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This? This right here? This is the problem. People are quick to find fault with YB, but fail to realize that the Euro-Americans are often being really, really unreasonable and putting up an &quot;our way or else&quot; system that &quot;just happens&quot; to have bad to lethal results for people who live in other ways.<br /> <br /> Yeah, sure it &quot;just happens&quot; to. Look who made it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, it's not &quot;euro-americans&quot;. The whole &quot;caern and surrounding territory are taken over&quot; is basically garou history worldwide. <br /> <br /> So the other tribes taking over the americas' caern is basically what a race of warriors have always done. And they justify it by simply reminding the loser, if they're still alive, that by losing to them, they proved they were unfit to guard this most holy place.<br /> <br /> The ways of the wyrmbringers are the same as the ways of the pure landers.<br /> <br /> And the wendigo of the modern age aren't oppressed by the other tribes. They're either member of multi tribal septs or control their own isolated septs where strangers are either forbidden or at best allowed on a one to one basis.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mywifeisscary is right that the wendigo are written like an antagonistic tribe. They bring nothing to the protagonist tribes that isn't provided by the uktena. And they are hostile to absolutly everyone even said uktena. Even the red talons aren't that anti everyone in the garou nation.<br /> <br /> <br /> And we know the wendigo don't have to behave that way because we have another still living native american tribe, the uktena. Which are cooperating with other tribes, are protecting natives, both american and around the world. And aren't defined by hatred.<br /> <br /> The uktena, by their own success, shows that the modern day wendigo's suffering is mostly self inflicted.<br /> \u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T15:57:45-07:00","id":1513471,"title":"","content":"I think one of the issues we\u2019re having is one of setting-framing versus story-framing and treating the one as equivalent to the other and as contradictory or overruling the other.<br /> <br /> I agree that the setting-framing of the Garou Nation\u2019s attitude towards Younger Brother is \u201cshut up and get over it\u201d.<br /> <br /> The thing is that one part of what I (and I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> ) are saying is that there is strong storytelling material in having a tribe (Younger Brother) who can respond to that and say, \u201cNo, fuck you\u201d.<br /> <br /> Having Older Brother and the themes of that tribe shouldn\u2019t displace Younger Brother because while they share a similar background, the difference in their response is important and imo the game benefits from having both, with the respective virtues and flaws of both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T16:48:01-07:00","id":1513480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513468#post1513468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is, it's not &quot;euro-americans&quot;. The whole &quot;caern and surrounding territory are taken over&quot; is basically garou history worldwide.<br /> <br /> So the other tribes taking over the americas' caern is basically what a race of warriors have always done. And they justify it by simply reminding the loser, if they're still alive, that by losing to them, they proved they were unfit to guard this most holy place.<br /> <br /> The ways of the wyrmbringers are the same as the ways of the pure landers.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Are they, though? that was not the arrangement between the three brothers. They did not take each others Caerns and had a pretty solid mutual working relationship (see Croatan Song). And even if they were, that does not make it right. The Garou have done a ton of shit to everyone and it's one of the things that they need to work on. Justifying yourself by saying &quot;that's how it's always been done&quot; is what got them into the shitstew they are in now. They need to do better and they can do better as we've seen throughout Revised.<br /> <br /> And Uktena didn't play ball. They chose to take many cultural and ethnic group as their kin and spread around the world to raise their own resilience as a tribe and find the things they always needed to know. In a way they played the wyrmcomers game by infiltrating places where the other Garou weren't established yet or took over places without defenders (and I assume at times removed some defenders, too).<br /> <br /> Wendigo on the other hand stayed home to guard their own lands and protect their kin. They got a front row seat to the the treatment of their kin - wolf and man - by the colonists. And it was a horrorshow all of its own. If anyone has a right to hold a grudge it's the Wendigo. The plot they are about is how to stop them from going too far and channel their righteous rage into something useful instead of taking themselves out. This is why the fences need to be mended and why amends need to be made. The battles in front of the Nation are way too big to keep insisting that just because it was good enough for someoen else it's good enough for us.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T18:27:49-07:00","id":1513491,"title":"","content":"Maybe I'm reading too much into it, but I think in Revised the Wendigo got the diversity increase it was in need. The Hoops' views got a bit of more focus and the page 37 highlighted the importance of the Old Gaian Way. The book also develops how they associate the white color with the disdain towards the Old Gaian Way and how there are &quot;a lot of red skins with white souls&quot; out there.<br /> <br /> It's still racist, they associate white with this dismantling of their traditional way of life, close to the land (no matter how harsh the land is), respecting the nature's cycles and honoring your prey. However there are camps in the tribe seeking to teach to those who are truly interested in their ways. IMHO this is the way to go with them in the modern nights without tearing the tribal culture away from them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1876-fenixpp","name":"Fenixpp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T00:49:06-07:00","id":1513508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513446#post1513446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This? This right here? This is the problem. People are quick to find fault with YB, but fail to realize that the Euro-Americans are often being really, really unreasonable and putting up an &quot;our way or else&quot; system that &quot;just happens&quot; to have bad to lethal results for people who live in other ways.<br /> <br /> Yeah, sure it &quot;just happens&quot; to. Look who made it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stag Tribes lost the majority of their caerns to fenrir, shadow lords, etc etc in the migration period. Are they bitter about it? yeah, but does it get in the way of modern cooperation? It does not. Granted, that was fifteen to twelve hundred hundred years ago, and it was the norm of the time, while Wendigo's loss is far more recent (still before anyone today was born) and quicker.<br /> <br /> Still, were the wendigo living in peace and harmony with the Croatan and Uktena? That's something really unlikely. How does such a massive continent have only three tribes when europe, a much smaller place, has at least five tribes distrinct to european regions and a bunch of other tribes spread throughout. Aboriginal Americans weren't some monolith. We know that before Europeans arrived in the Americas that the locals very often fought one another, and indeed european trade gave some tribes a big advantage over others that they happily exploited. <br /> <br /> You have two options: can you reasonably conclude that the Wendigo, Uktena and Croatan got their dominant position by killing rivals and supressing dissidents; or you can relish in a pleasing fiction where natives are patronizingly exonerated as pure and wonderful noble savages who lived in peace and harmony in some kind of continent wide triatic balance before the white devils ruined everything. <br /> <br /> The Uktena rolled with it. They looked at their situation through the lens of a realist and adapted. The Wendigo didn't, not because they suffered more or because they can't have smart people in the tribe, but because... they were written by a white American who wanted to make a persistent statement about colonialism. This is compounded further when you realize every tribe has a particular focus to bring to the player pack and while the Wendigo certainly have some fun stealth combinations early on the other tribe gifts are mid and don't combine well (like why the fuck would they have <i>Heroes Stand</i>? All their best gifts are about being sneaky bastards, they don't have anything that supports standing in the same spot for some physical bonuses. This is some NPC thinking right here) . But a lot of other tribes have fun stealth gifts too and character wise the Red Talons do all the emo shit better. They weren't built to fit with the player pack, they're an NPC tribe. <br /> <br /> The entire tribe is some white-guilt fetish. Which is weird for me because: <br /> 1- I didn't do anything wrong<br /> 2- My ancestors very probably didn't do anything wrong (in colonial respects at least) <br /> 3-I'm sure 1 and 2 apply to a lot of white people<br /> 4- Expecting people to feel bad because of their colour of their skin meets the definition of racism<br /> 5- And this one can't be understated: I don't think the Wendigo represent native american attitudes. Given that natives have found the tribe offensive and launched complaints, I think that's pretty certain. <br /> <br /> Yeah, the Wendigo are fucking unreasonable, particularly because they were written as a cheap white-guilt shit-fling rather than a possible society. Nobody is saying the British and French empires or the 13 colonies were saints, but the tension between the wendigo and literally everybody else is excessive and na\u00efve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T01:09:52-07:00","id":1513510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513215#post1513215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> RE: Little Brother, it's difficult to be racist when you aren't the ones in power, since that typically relies on being able to force others to accede to your wishes and then imposing a system on them. It requires going along with the system in power, which is not really something most of them do. If they did, they wouldn't be struggling and dying. It'd probably be better to focus Little Brother's troubles on other issues with the predicament of their kin.</div> </div> </div> </div>No it's very easy to be racist when you're not the ones in power. Forgive me for frothing at the mouth with rage, but It's asinine bullshit like this that make &quot;liberals&quot; look like a joke. Power isn't some absolutist concept where just because the president is white, the police are white, and the rich are white, it becomes impossible for a black man to abuse a white man. Having actually lived in minority areas and lived in areas I can actually tell you with certainty that no, there isn't any immunity. I've endured enough sexist and racist bullshit to be livid at someone telling me it's &quot;difficult&quot; to be racist towards me. This idea that it's OK to be racist towards majority groups is only counterproductive. All it earns is resentment and further perpetuation of racist stereotyping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T01:34:21-07:00","id":1513511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513510#post1513510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No it's very easy to be racist when you're not the ones in power. Forgive me for frothing at the mouth with rage, but It's asinine bullshit like this that make &quot;liberals&quot; look like a joke. Power isn't some absolutist concept where just because the president is white, the police are white, and the rich are white, it becomes impossible for a black man to abuse a white man. Having actually lived in minority areas and lived in areas I can actually tell you with certainty that no, there isn't any immunity. I've endured enough sexist and racist bullshit to be livid at someone telling me it's &quot;difficult&quot; to be racist towards me. This idea that it's OK to be racist towards majority groups is only counterproductive. All it earns is resentment and further perpetuation of racist stereotyping.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think a lot of people online get jumbled up with institutional racism vs personal racism. Its why you get statements like &quot;you cant be racist against x.&quot;. Its an odd misunderstanding you see online because nobody actually reads up on the nuances of arguements.<br /> <br /> As a side racists are pretty much guaranteed to present themselves as the wronged disenfranchised party which only complicates matters further.<br /> <br /> To lead back to the wendigo/little brother I tend to consider them racist on a personal level since theyre characterised as disenfranchised. What could be interesting could be if they started to gain prestige and power in a first nation context and start using that power for low key institutional racism in contrast to older brothers more forgive and forget outlook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T02:49:45-07:00","id":1513515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513511#post1513511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think a lot of people online get jumbled up with institutional racism vs personal racism. Its why you get statements like &quot;you cant be racist against x.&quot;. Its an odd misunderstanding you see online because nobody actually reads up on the nuances of arguements.<br /> <br /> <br /> As a side racists are pretty much guaranteed to present themselves as the wronged disenfranchised party which only complicates matters further.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;online&quot;<br /> No, it's a bit more mainstream than that, you see it on the news, at least in the west. When you see someone be racist and then say &quot;my people can't be racist&quot; it's aggravating. Now I know full well that the media takes the actions of small groups of people and blows them out of proportion, but the bulk of people aren't academics and the lowest common denominator is more important in this field.<br /> <br /> As for institutional racism vs personal racism, and how racists are pretty much garanteed to present themselves as the wronged disenfranchised party...<br /> Well yeah. This is actually one area where the Right has better evidence. Institutionalized racism like, say, police bias against black Americans is a nebulous and convoluted mess of arguments and counterarguments and it's messy enough to plausibly deny. On the other hand, if you look at say, the privileges granted to Australian Aboriginals and Torres strait islanders, it's written down in law, clear in black and white, that they get benefits white Australians don't. That's very clear institutionalized racism, and evidence of a group of people being wronged and disenfranchised; never mind that these privileges are granted in an effort to bring Aboriginal/Torres strait islanders into the living standards that white Australians enjoy after decades of exclusionary practices. In the developed world, there are no laws that explicitly disenfranchise minority citizen, they have all been done away with, so your average Joe doesn't see a campaign for equal rights, they see a campaign for extra rights.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To lead back to the wendigo/little brother I tend to consider them racist on a personal level since theyre characterised as disenfranchised. What could be interesting could be if they started to gain prestige and power in a first nation context and start using that power for low key institutional racism in contrast to older brothers more forgive and forget outlook. </div> </div> </div>The whole tribe is fucking racist; what do you mean &quot;on a personal level&quot;? like the parents teach the kids on mass to hate the white devil what part of that isn't institutional? A tribe is an institution! If you were a white wendigo and wanted to learn rites your prospective teacher would be pressured out of it. is that institutional racism or is that just an excessive amount of personal racism: does it make a difference?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 06-01-2023, 06:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T03:12:42-07:00","id":1513517,"title":"","content":"That's....quite the response for a post which was genrally in agreement with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T03:54:38-07:00","id":1513519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513517#post1513517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's....quite the response for a post which was genrally in agreement with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, well, maybe I was a little incensed... and there are some parts I still very much disagree with you on. Anyhow, I went to edit it to tone it down but then it got picked up as spam cuz this site is a joke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T06:20:53-07:00","id":1513528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513511#post1513511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> To lead back to the wendigo/little brother I tend to consider them racist on a personal level since theyre characterised as disenfranchised. What could be interesting could be if they started to gain prestige and power in a first nation context and start using that power for low key institutional racism in contrast to older brothers more forgive and forget outlook.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the wendigo as an organisation is institutionally racist. The whole anti white narrative is weaved into the way the tribe sees strangers and discriminates toward potential recruits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T15:41:56-07:00","id":1513571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513510#post1513510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No it's very easy to be racist when you're not the ones in power. Forgive me for frothing at the mouth with rage, but It's asinine bullshit like this that make &quot;liberals&quot; look like a joke. Power isn't some absolutist concept where just because the president is white, the police are white, and the rich are white, it becomes impossible for a black man to abuse a white man. Having actually lived in minority areas and lived in areas I can actually tell you with certainty that no, there isn't any immunity. I've endured enough sexist and racist bullshit to be livid at someone telling me it's &quot;difficult&quot; to be racist towards me. This idea that it's OK to be racist towards majority groups is only counterproductive. All it earns is resentment and further perpetuation of racist stereotyping.</div> </div> </div> </div>Institutional power is a vital ingredient of the mix. Without it, you only have bigots that are prejudiced. Racism is entire apparatus constructed over several centuries across a number of different countries. It has the machinery of oppression on its side. Being racist is going along with that machinery. This is not some new notion; it was a popular codification in online discourse a decade ago. Other forms of institutionalized prejudice fall into the mix as well; it's why we get medical studied that frequently don't use any of the prospective subjects in question, no matter the group (my axe to grind here is with thyroid treatment, incidentally).<br /> <br /> Also, I didn't say it was &quot;okay to be prejudiced against majority groups&quot;. I cited the existence of the above looming machinery, and how, as noted, unless someone is going along with it, they aren't racist. That doesn't rule out other forms of prejudice. Where this applies to Younger Brother is that they are factually bitter and not usually willing to accept help... because very often, &quot;help&quot; that was offered wasn't. You have to offer aid on the terms of another, or it's not aid, it's just cramming more shit down their throat. The well-meaning but clueless can be a greater danger than they realize. Whether or not they're rude about rebuffing &quot;insistence&quot; is another matter entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T15:46:52-07:00","id":1513574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513571#post1513571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Institutional power is a vital ingredient of the mix. Without it, you only have bigots that are prejudiced. Racism is entire apparatus constructed over several centuries across a number of different countries. It has the machinery of oppression on its side. Being racist is going along with that machinery. This is not some new notion; it was a popular codification in online discourse a decade ago. Other forms of institutionalized prejudice fall into the mix as well; it's why we get medical studied that frequently don't use any of the prospective subjects in question, no matter the group (my axe to grind here is with thyroid treatment, incidentally).<br /> <br /> Also, I didn't say it was &quot;okay to be prejudiced against majority groups&quot;. I cited the existence of the above looming machinery, and how, as noted, unless someone is going along with it, they aren't racist. That doesn't rule out other forms of prejudice. Where this applies to Younger Brother is that they are factually bitter and not usually willing to accept help... because very often, &quot;help&quot; that was offered wasn't. You have to offer aid on the terms of another, or it's not aid, it's just cramming more shit down their throat. The well-meaning but clueless can be a greater danger than they realize. Whether or not they're rude about rebuffing &quot;insistence&quot; is another matter entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> What? Racism is prejudice based on race. It doesn't requires institutional power. Someone is prejudiced against someone based on race criteria, it's racism.<br /> <br /> That's the point of the concept of institutional racism. If there's a need to precise &quot;institutional&quot;, it's because it's not a fundamental part of the very idea of racism.<br /> <br /> Tldr, racism is not an apparatus, it's a human behavior that exist both with and without institutions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T15:53:20-07:00","id":1513575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513574#post1513574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> What? Racism is prejudice based on race. It doesn't requires institutional power. Someone is prejudiced against someone based on race criteria, it's racism.<br /> <br /> That's the point of the concept of institutional racism. If there's a need to precise &quot;institutional&quot;, it's because it's not a fundamental part of the very idea of racism.<br /> <br /> Tldr, racism is not an apparatus, it's a human behavior that exist both with and without institutions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you not pay attention to this not exactly being a new working definition in the same post that you just quoted? Don't obstinately dig your feet in and say &quot;nuh uh!&quot; when someone defines what their use of a word is. Especially not when it's not just their use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T18:13:08-07:00","id":1513588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513575#post1513575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did you not pay attention to this not exactly being a new working definition in the same post that you just quoted? Don't obstinately dig your feet in and say &quot;nuh uh!&quot; when someone defines what their use of a word is. Especially not when it's not just their use.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> people can say they use a new shiny definition. But they can't argue with it when the validity of said definition isn't enssured and people keep using the original definition.<br /> <br /> So you can say that you believe that racism required institutional backing. But you can't state it as fact over and over again.<br /> <br /> And the idea that racism is by essence institutional IS a new definition. And a very narrow one seeing how it barely exist outside of the usa and american influenced academia","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T18:31:19-07:00","id":1513590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513588#post1513588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> people can say they use a new shiny definition. But they can't argue with it when the validity of said definition isn't enssured and people keep using the original definition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stipulative introduced in 1970, and it's been making the rounds on the internet for at least the last 10 years. That's not really shiny and new by linguistic standards, given that language can and often does change underfoot like the Flux Realm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So you can say that you believe that racism required institutional backing. But you can't state it as fact over and over again. </div> </div> </div>Words are only what we make of them. I already gave notice about how I'd be using language; ignoring it and acting like it isn't how I'm using language is not a good way to go.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the idea that racism is by essence institutional IS a new definition. And a very narrow one seeing how it barely exist outside of the usa and american influenced academia </div> </div> </div>Conveniently, in talking about the Pure Ones, we're necessarily narrowing our view to the Americas. As such, I'm not seeing a huge problem with using this framework in the context of the Three Brothers of W:tA and who remains of them in modern days.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T19:09:03-07:00","id":1513594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513590#post1513590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Stipulative introduced in 1970, and it's been making the rounds on the internet for at least the last 10 years. That's not really shiny and new by linguistic standards, given that language can and often does change underfoot like the Flux Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is basically yesterday, the word racism is at least centuries old. Plus, your definition is, as I said, extremely liimited in it's application geographically and culturally. You may be finding people agreeing with you in the usa and canada (and even there, mostly within academic grounds), but you will be hard pressed to find a french, mexican or japanese using it rather than affirming that racism simply means prejudice based on race.<br /> <br /> QUOTE=Saur Ops Specialist;n1513590]<br /> Words are only what we make of them. I already gave notice about how I'd be using language; ignoring it and acting like it isn't how I'm using language is not a good way to go.<br /> [/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Words are used collectively. You can say you will be using a common word in a way most people won't be using it. But you can't then expect people to take your definition as the right one during a discussion. Which is what you were doing by &quot;correcting&quot; people for &quot;forgetting&quot; that racism is institutional by essence as if it was a fact and not a new definition that you use.<br /> <br /> QUOTE=Saur Ops Specialist;n1513590]<br /> Conveniently, in talking about the Pure Ones, we're necessarily narrowing our view to the Americas. As such, I'm not seeing a huge problem with using this framework in the context of the Three Brothers of W:tA and who remains of them in modern days.<br /> [/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> The idea of racism, like all concepts, is not limited to the americas, what is or is not racism does not change depending on whenether the topic is native americans, chineses or russians.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T19:26:59-07:00","id":1513597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513571#post1513571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Institutional power is a vital ingredient of the mix. Without it, you only have bigots that are prejudiced. Racism is entire apparatus constructed over several centuries across a number of different countries. It has the machinery of oppression on its side. Being racist is going along with that machinery. This is not some new notion; it was a popular codification in online discourse a decade ago. Other forms of institutionalized prejudice fall into the mix as well; it's why we get medical studied that frequently don't use any of the prospective subjects in question, no matter the group (my axe to grind here is with thyroid treatment, incidentally).</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen that definition before (Racism = Power + Prejudice) but it's not one I agree with because it ends up being arbitrary.<br /> <br /> Let's take the example of Joe, a white guy in the United States. He hates Chinese people and says horrible things about Chinese people. Joe is very clearly bigoted and is racist because he's a white guy in the US and in the US white people have had a ton of institutional power to oppress Chinese people. Joe gets on an airplane and moves to China. Joe says the same stuff about Chinese people there. Joe is still bigoted, he still says the exact same things he did a a few hours ago in the US, but he's no longer racist. As a white person in China he's not part of the group that maintains or holds institutional power.<br /> <br /> This means that whether someone can be considered racist isn't determined by <i>what</i> they say or <i>what</i> they do, but rather it's determined by the geographical location in which they say or do those things and then only if they're part of the racial/ethnic group that holds power in that geographical location. Someone screaming the n-word could stop being racist in the middle of their screeching simply because they stepped across a national or geographic border in the middle of their tirade and went from being part of an ethnic group with institutional power in one country to an ethnic group with no institutional power in another.<br /> <br /> Personally I believe that trying to define racism in that way is garbage. IMO that definition of racism was simply created so that minorities could say or do things that would be considered racist if white people said or did them and then they could say, &quot;No, no, I'm not racist. It's okay for me to say that because I'm not a white person (and therefore don't have political power and nothing I do or say can be considered racist).&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T20:09:04-07:00","id":1513600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513597#post1513597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> Personally I believe that trying to define racism in that way is garbage. IMO that definition of racism was simply created so that minorities could say or do things that would be considered racist if white people said or did them and then they could say, &quot;No, no, I'm not racist. It's okay for me to say that because I'm not a white person (and therefore don't have political power and nothing I do or say can be considered racist).&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to agree with that conclusion. In my experience, the &quot;racism is power+prejudice&quot; line generally comes to sort of justify a racist takes against people that aren't considered a minority.<br /> <br /> Which is exactly what is happening here, since the concept is used to sort of justify the racist behavior of the wendigo.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T01:33:51-07:00","id":1513622,"title":"","content":"The ultimate issue with trying to restrain racism to a pure institutional construct is its Ineligant and counter intuitive. It provides no benifit to the disenfranchised nor a meaningful critique of the oppressor. If anything it muddies the water on a number of levels in terms of racism by allowing bigots some semantic wriggle room or an easy dunk for rhetoric.<br /> <br /> At best pointless more likely out right self defeating","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T04:44:04-07:00","id":1513632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513571#post1513571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Institutional power is a vital ingredient of the mix. Without it, you only have bigots that are prejudiced. Racism is entire apparatus constructed over several centuries across a number of different countries. It has the machinery of oppression on its side. Being racist is going along with that machinery. This is not some new notion; it was a popular codification in online discourse a decade ago. Other forms of institutionalized prejudice fall into the mix as well; it's why we get medical studied that frequently don't use any of the prospective subjects in question, no matter the group (my axe to grind here is with thyroid treatment, incidentally).</div> </div> </div> </div>I say this as a liberal arts major: this is wank. A select few big heads getting together in a small room does not qualify as a consensus. Racism is not the an entire apparatus, racism is racism as the dictionary and common thought dictate it to be. Do I need to be an etymologist to explain 'race' and 'ism' not necessitating some kind of 'apparatus'. Racism isn't power+prejudice, that's a fallacy. Racism is, if I look up a definition: <i>prejudice, discrimination, or antagonism by an individual, community, or institution against a person or people on the basis of their membership of a particular racial or ethnic group.</i> There's also the definition of it being a belief, but in neither case is there the idea that we need at least an institutional racism before we have 'real' racism. <br /> <br /> If I drop racial slurs and call everyone subhuman, but do it in Nairobi where I am not representative of the ruling populace, am I committing a racist act or am I shielded from the racist label because I'm not a member of institutional power and the 'apparatus'? That's preposterous. Quit the mental gymnastics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T06:16:52-07:00","id":1513641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513600#post1513600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I tend to agree with that conclusion. In my experience, the &quot;racism is power+prejudice&quot; line generally comes to sort of justify a racist takes against people that aren't considered a minority.<br /> <br /> Which is exactly what is happening here, since the concept is used to sort of justify the racist behavior of the wendigo.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd already shifted to the metatext, if you want to get back to that. You know, the metatext where there was no native input and the tribe ended up looking worse than the Swords of Heimdall, according to you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T07:25:07-07:00","id":1513644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513641#post1513641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd already shifted to the metatext, if you want to get back to that. You know, the metatext where there was no native input and the tribe ended up looking worse than the Swords of Heimdall, according to you?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd strongly contend that the Tribe is a lot less bad than the sword. Bitterness over centuries of ethinic cleansing is a considerable number of degrees from litteral nazis. Even if the wendigo are complete bastards it's a reaction to oppression not a inherant genocidal inclination.<br /> <br /> Although you have a point native American cultural experts would have been a massive positive. It might even have been wise to approach specific first nation tribes rather than just general first nation Canadians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-02-2023, 11:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T07:36:16-07:00","id":1513646,"title":"","content":"Thinking on it further if we were to bring the croatan back into this they could form a mid way point between the other two groups focussing on moderate protectionism in contrast to older and younger brother. &quot;We will work with you and don't hold you accountable but you will never be one of us.&quot; Vibe.<br /> <br /> You could even develop the tribes by having them establishing tentative footholds in other disenfranchised peoples such as the ainu and sami and creating kinfolk in those communities. It also provides a nice reason for European members of the Tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T08:13:13-07:00","id":1513647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513641#post1513641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd already shifted to the metatext, if you want to get back to that. You know, the metatext where there was no native input and the tribe ended up looking worse than the Swords of Heimdall, according to you?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a non sequitur take. The authors not being native isn't what made the wendigo the equivalent of the swords of heimdall. Proof being that the same authors made the wendigo, which aren't a racist tribe.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T08:15:32-07:00","id":1513648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513646#post1513646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could even develop the tribes by having them establishing tentative footholds in other disenfranchised peoples such as the ainu and sami and creating kinfolk in those communities. It also provides a nice reason for European members of the Tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's technically what the uktena are since revised edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T08:45:14-07:00","id":1513653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513648#post1513648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's technically what the uktena are since revised edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah i was thinking of dividing it into a three way however. We're all three zone on areas of sympathy. The uktena being the most extreme and taking anyone vs the more Conservative wendigo or hypothetical croatan.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T12:02:28-07:00","id":1513676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513644#post1513644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd strongly contend that the Tribe is a lot less bad than the sword.</div> </div> </div> </div>As would I, but apparently there's some strong fixation in the thread to make YB out to be really, really terrible. Like, notably worse than other Garou tribes that are also obsessed with bloodline purity, such as the Silver Fangs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bitterness over centuries of ethinic cleansing is a considerable number of degrees from litteral nazis. Even if the wendigo are complete bastards it's a reaction to oppression not a inherant genocidal inclination. </div> </div> </div>I would similarly contend that they're too sympathetic to be total bastards. Especially if they have a strong Ancestors rating; they'll be re-living the trauma of centuries of colonialism with great frequency. Mokole with Mnesis are in a similar boat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Although you have a point native American cultural experts would have been a massive positive. It might even have been wise to approach specific first nation tribes rather than just general first nation Canadians. </div> </div> </div>I'm having a bit of difficulty parsing the difference that you're establishing between the consultants. Can you explain again?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T12:50:41-07:00","id":1513687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513676#post1513676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm having a bit of difficulty parsing the difference that you're establishing between the consultants. Can you explain again?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's just a guess, but I believe he is referring to having a consultant could help in the sense that he could ensure that the tribe is not portrayed negatively or stereotyped as an indigenous tribe, thus avoiding offending the group, pointing out mistakes and giving advice basically and preventing the writer from exaggerating, although if that's the case I believe it's not that simple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T07:49:14-07:00","id":1513770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513676#post1513676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As would I, but apparently there's some strong fixation in the thread to make YB out to be really, really terrible. Like, notably worse than other Garou tribes that are also obsessed with bloodline purity, such as the Silver Fangs.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're all happy to acknowledge that Silver Fangs are pieces of shit and I imagine that a majority of us would agree they shouldn't lead the Garou nation. We're happy to acknowledge that Red Talons are fools and that the Get Of Fenrir are perfect Garou and that's their greatest flaw. But that's the thing... we're not at all contentious on the subject so it's not really worth discussing Red Talon flaws since we all know and agree on them. <br /> <br /> The wendigo would probably be <i>less </i>flawed than the other tribes were it not their unique position: most tribes have rivalries but get along well enough with most other tribes with a few oil-and-water cases like GW/RT. The Wendigo are adversarial to the <i>majority</i> of tribes. When your Tribe's best ally is the Red Talons, you know you have problems. Most tribes are defined by something more than just a cultural origin, and the Wendigo are defined by... not liking the rest of the tribes. It's not a matter of them being native American or not (Uktena are one of my favourites) if the Wendigo were Siberian or Saami or Japanese or Ethiopian they'd still be a questionable inclusion as the tribe who doesn't like the other tribes. The part where they're a racist caricature poorly made to critique colonialism is a separate (though still very important) matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T08:28:38-07:00","id":1513777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512700-core-themes-of-the-tribes-for-a-better-w5?p=1513676#post1513676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As would I, but apparently there's some strong fixation in the thread to make YB out to be really, really terrible. Like, notably worse than other Garou tribes that are also obsessed with bloodline purity, such as the Silver Fangs.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really a fixation, but simply the logical conclusion of the behavior of the tribe.<br /> <br /> The problem with the wendigo isn't that there are racist, after all, many groups in ttrpg, even protagonist groups, are deeply flawed, and it's not a problem in itself for entertainment, after all &quot;dwarves and elves hates each others&quot; is an appreciated trope in fantasy for a reason.<br /> <br /> The problem is that this hate of strangers is the main and I would dare to say only defining trait of the tribe.<br /> <br /> To make a comparison with elves and dwarves. Each of those species have typically many traits separating them from other groups in fantasy, be it the timeless and extremely sophisticated elven society or the sturdy, proud and crafty one of the dwarves. Their despise or the other is one trait only.<br /> <br /> Now look at the wendigo. What define them? Basically that they're a mystical group protecting sacred ground, that they're native american and that they hates non natives.<br /> <br /> But compared to the other playable groups of the game, this doesn't really identify them. All garou tribes are mystical people protecting their sacred ground (maybe silent striders excluded), and two other tribes were native american.<br /> <br /> So you end up with having only their racism as a defining trait. <br /> <br /> Which is a problem they share with the red talons. I don't remember who, but someone on the forum was pretty on point showing that the red talons traits are their hatred of humans and their lupine perception of the world, but that the later was common to every lupus population in any tribe, which let us with the RT only being specific by their misanthropy.<br /> <br /> That's a problem avoided by the third of the &quot;prejudice triat&quot; of werewolf, the black furies. Which, while being defined in great part by they misandry, are saved by having other deep characteristics, such as being the only tribe wholly devoted to the wyld, and by being tied to ancient greece myth, something no other tribe has.<br /> <br /> TLDR: you can have a playable faction that is deeply prejudiced, but such prejudice must not be the only trait separating from other factions.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}